2026-09-27T11:19:52.9618436Z Update Note
2026-09-27T11:19:52.9618972Z ===========
2026-09-27T11:19:52.9619781Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T11:19:52.9620599Z 
2026-09-27T11:19:52.9620864Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T11:19:52.9621460Z ================
2026-09-27T11:19:52.9621810Z 
2026-09-27T11:19:52.9622260Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T11:19:52.9623351Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T11:19:52.9623981Z 
2026-09-27T11:19:52.9624289Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T11:19:52.9625103Z ====================================
2026-09-27T11:19:52.9625642Z 
2026-09-27T11:19:52.9626009Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T11:19:52.9627334Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T11:19:52.9628408Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T11:19:52.9630473Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T11:19:52.9632209Z 
2026-09-27T11:19:52.9632523Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T11:19:52.9633793Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T11:19:52.9635410Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T11:19:52.9636273Z 
2026-09-27T11:19:52.9637335Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T11:19:52.9638608Z 
2026-09-27T11:19:52.9638851Z Packages
2026-09-27T11:19:52.9639398Z ========
2026-09-27T11:19:52.9639724Z 
2026-09-27T11:19:52.9642037Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T11:19:52.9644351Z 
2026-09-27T11:19:52.9644738Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T11:19:52.9645634Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T11:19:52.9647159Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T11:19:52.9648162Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T11:19:52.9649103Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T11:19:52.9649797Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T11:19:52.9650392Z 
2026-09-27T11:19:52.9650563Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T11:19:52.9650964Z ==========================
2026-09-27T11:19:52.9651206Z 
2026-09-27T11:19:52.9652988Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T11:19:52.9654862Z 
2026-09-27T11:19:52.9655980Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T11:19:52.9657650Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T11:19:52.9658009Z 
